{"elites_ig(jap)" "This squad of 15 imperial guardsmen with 5 skill are adept at both defense and assault, in any terrain, with better equipment for defensive operations. Comes with 2 Type 99 LMG teams."}
{"elites_takasago(jap)" "This squad of 15 Takasago paratroopers of Taiwanese aboriginal ancestry with 6 skill are perfect for conducting special operations on the enemy. Comes with 2 Type 99 LMG teams."}
{"elites_drop(jap)" "A paradroppable squad of 15 elite Teishin marine paratroopers."}
{"elite_tankmans(jap)" "This elite tank crewman is only lightly armed but is very well-suited for crewing your armored vehicles and field guns. Use them to replace the losses you have suffered in combat and re-man your equipment. They are not suited for infantry combat and can't capture points."}
{"vehic_supporter(jap)" "Two support crew for re-crewing vehicles and field guns."}
{"type97(jap)" "Type 97 light tank - scout and infantry support. Useful HE; avoid medium tanks head-on."}
{"ho-ha3mgun(jap)" "Ho-Ha half-track with triple MGs - troop transport and suppressive fire. Keep moving; avoid AT fire."}
{"isuzutx40(jap)" "Isuzu truck - logistics and troop transport. Ideal for redeployment; fragile under fire."}
{"isuzutx40art(jap)" "Isuzu heavy ammo truck - resupplies artillery and heavy weapons. Keep behind the lines and protected."}
{"isuzutx40_eng(jap)" "Isuzu engineer truck - delivers construction and repair supplies. Guard against raids."}
{"type2_20mm(jap)" "20mm Type 2 AA gun - anti-air and anti-infantry. Excellent against planes and soft targets; avoid tanks."}
{"isuzutx40_aa(jap)" "Isuzu AA truck - mobile AA platform. Strong versus aircraft and light vehicles; very fragile."}
{"pak47(jap)" "47mm Type 1 AT gun - anti-tank sector anchor. Conceal, fire, and relocate."}
{"t90_75m(jap)" "75mm Type 90 field gun - direct and indirect fire support. Position with cover; watch counter-battery."}
{"isuzutx40_mort(jap)" "Isuzu mortar support truck - mobile indirect fire support. Fire and displace; very vulnerable."}
{"type_97_150mm(jap)" "150mm Type 97 mortar - heavy indirect fire. Devastating blasts; slow to move and easy to counter-battery."}
{"type4_200mm(jap)" "200mm Type 4 rocket mortar - massive area saturation. Site well behind the line and guard closely."}
{"t91_105m(jap)" "105mm Type 91 howitzer - general-purpose indirect fire. Provides standoff HE; beware counter-battery."}
{"ho-ni2(jap)" "Ho-Ni 2 SP howitzer - open-top assault gun for HE support. Avoid prolonged exposure to AT fire."}
{"ho-ro(jap)" "Ho-Ro SP howitzer - 150mm HE hammer. Devastating vs infantry and emplacements; paper-thin protection."}
{"ha-to(jap)" "Ha-To rocket artillery - heavy rocket system. Extreme area damage; keep far from the front and hidden."}
{"type93scout(jap)" "Type 92 armored car - reconnaissance and harassment. Fast with light armament; avoid heavy AT threats."}
{"ke-nu(jap)" "Ke-Nu light tank - incremental protection over early lights. Best used for screening and support."}
{"chi-ha57(jap)" "Chi-Ha - 57mm short gun for HE support. Weak AT performance; rely on flanks and ambush."}
{"chi-ha47(jap)" "Chi-Ha Kai - 47mm gun improves AT capability. Still a light tank; avoid head-on duels."}
{"ss-d(jap)" "Flamethrower tank detachment - bunker buster and trench clearer. Close-range only; protect from AT."}
{"chi-he(jap)" "Chi-He medium tank - balanced armor with 47mm gun. General support; avoid heavy AT lines."}
{"ho-i(jap)" "Ho-I medium support tank - 75mm howitzer for infantry support. Best against soft targets; mind AT threats."}
{"chi-nu(jap)" "Chi-Nu medium tank - 75mm long gun offers solid AP. Engage at range and use cover."}
{"chi-ha120(jap)" "SNLF Chi-Ha (120) - naval 120mm for heavy HE support. Fragile for its firepower; keep screened."}
{"chi-to(jap)" "Chi-To medium tank - late-war 75mm with good penetration. Excel at mid-long range; protect flanks."}
{"chi-ri(jap)" "Chi-Ri medium tank - larger chassis with strong gun and crew efficiency. Support pushes; avoid AT ambushes."}
{"ho-ni1(jap)" "Ho-Ni 1 tank destroyer - 75mm AT gun on open-top chassis. Ambush from cover; relocate after firing."}
{"ho-ni_3(jap)" "Ho-Ni 3 tank destroyer - enclosed casemate with 75mm. Better survivability; fight hull-down and at range."}
{"hero1_jap(jap)" "AT detachment with anti-armor assets screened by riflemen. Suited to ambush tanks at close-to-mid range; keep concealed until engagement."}
{"hero2_jap(jap)" "Kamikaze strike team for shock assaults and point denial. Extremely fast on foot; use surprise and cover to close distance."}
{"heronew1_jap(jap)" "Flamethrower tank package for bunker reduction and trench clearing. Devastating up close; highly vulnerable to AT weapons."}
{"heronew3_jap(jap)" "Heavy 150mm mortar package for indirect fire and area denial. Set well behind the line; relocate to avoid counter-battery."}
{"heronew2_jap(jap)" "Ho-Ni 3 tank destroyer package with crew. Enclosed 75mm casemate for safer AT support; fight from standoff and cover."}
{"hero8_jap(jap)" "SNLF Chi-Ha (120) package—naval 120mm for heavy HE support. Use for breaching and suppression; avoid direct AT duels."}
{"hero6_jap(jap)" "Chi-He hero tank with crew—balanced medium for general support. Engage mediums with positioning; avoid heavy AT lines."}
{"hero7_jap(jap)" "Mobile rocket artillery package with transport. Employ shoot-and-scoot tactics; keep far from enemy scouts and AT."}
{"hero9_jap(jap)" "Ho-Ri 1 heavy tank destroyer package—powerful long gun for first-shot kills. Keep hull-down and avoid artillery saturation."}
{"banzai_1(jap)" "Banzai chargers—15-man melee-focused assault squad. Repeated-buy hero sequence enables sequential buys of individual squads for free. Inital - 1 squad, 15 min - 2 squads, 30 mins - 4 squads, 45 mins - 8 squads, 60 mins - 16 squads. Notably high stamina and strong sprint; best for shock assaults, point flooding, and tying down enemy lines."}
